{
  "title": "Vernier laser mode hop",
  "group": "Lasers & modulators",
  "description": "Vernier laser from NOISE, with a live mode hop: SOA + ASE injector + two 5-mode ring combs (R = 400/425 µm → FSR 29.8/28.1 GHz, ΔFSR = 1.76 GHz ~ 1.5 linewidths). The SOA's deterministic seed is OFF — broadband ASE (-135 dBm/Hz, the physical n_sp·hν·(G−1)) seeds EVERY comb line; three alignment candidates start above threshold at t = 0.3 ns, compete for the shared gain, and the aligned pair at 1310 nm wins and clamps it. At t = 6 ns the ring-B heater steps 0.50 V (0.50 mW = a 1.76 GHz comb shift) WHILE THE LASER RUNS: the running mode falls below threshold, p_out collapses while the reservoir refills, and the newly aligned pair one FSR (29.8 GHz, ×17 Vernier lever) to the red grows out of the ASE floor and takes over — watch the two lines at 1310.00 and 1310.17 nm on the OSA spectrum. Takes several minutes: 48k solver steps resolve the ±60 GHz beats of the losing modes The pinned physics study is examples/soa_vernier_laser.py.",
  "analysis": {
    "mode": "transient",
    "t_stop": 1.2e-08,
    "points": 6000,
    "dtmax": 2.5e-13,
    "noise": {
      "seeds": 1,
      "bw": 500000000000.0
    }
  },
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 20,
        "y": -173,
        "title": "Vernier laser mode hop — what this testbench does",
        "lines": [
          "Pulse VP1 biases SOA1; injector ASE1 (-135 dBm/Hz) seeds",
          "every comb line with broadband noise (SOA seed off).",
          "Two Vernier ring combs RC1 (400 um) and RC2 (425 um) have",
          "slightly different FSR; only aligned pairs reach threshold,",
          "and the pair at 1310 nm wins and clamps the shared gain.",
          "At t = 6 ns heater VH steps 0.50 V, shifting RC2's comb:",
          "the running mode drops out and a new aligned pair takes",
          "over. p_out (spectrum) shows the mode hop on the OSA.",
          "",
          "Set VH.V = 0 and re-run: no comb shift, so no mode hop."
        ]
      }
    ],
